HARD FACTS & EVENTS:
- A lawyer paid a lawyer to obtain an advisory ethics opinion (No. 2016-04) allowing a Fairhope Airport Board member to lease with the airport authority, whose partner is the Municipal Judge for Fairhope.
- On August 7, 2015, three board members resigned and Joe McEnerey was appointed Chairman, Pam Caudill as Vice Chair, and Ray Hix as Secretary/Treasurer by the Airport Authority.
- Ray Hix became privileged to confidential information regarding airport leases, bids, and financial information after his appointment.
- Ray Hix proceeded to secure a lease as Mid Bay Air LLC despite holding a position on the Board with access to non-public financial data.
- The Fairhope Airport Authority signed a memorandum of lease with Mid-Bay Air LLC on December 23, 2015, prior to the issuance of any Ethics Opinion.
- Jack Burrell, the City Council President and Airport Authority Board Member, chaired an ad hoc committee that reviewed bids and determined his associate board member was the winner.
- On November 8, 2016, a request was sent to the Alabama Ethics Commission asking for written remarks regarding the Mid-Bay Air Lease awarded around December 2015 at Sonny Callahan Airport in Fairhope.
- On December 2, 2016, the Alabama Ethics Commission replied that no lease had ever been submitted to them regarding this issue.
- The Ethics Opinion stated that a copy of any contract/lease agreement entered into between the Board member and the Airport Authority must be filed with the Alabama Ethics Commission within ten days of entry.

AUTHOR'S ALLEGATION:
The author alleges that Jack Burrell failed to prevent an obvious conflict of interest by allowing Ray Hix, who had access to confidential airport information as a board member, to sign a lease for Mid Bay Air LLC; the author contends the lease is null and void because it was signed before an ethics opinion was filed and requires immediate resignation.

