free-speech.compressed:
HARD FACTS & EVENTS:
- Hurricane Irma was expected to make landfall in the Miami area and travel through Florida.
- Baldwin County is geographically centered between hurricanes Harvey and Irma, leading to an influx of storm immigrants.
- The Fairhope City Council was scheduled to meet on September 11, 2001 (noted as Monday Sept 11th in text), at 6:00 pm in City Council Chambers to decide who is allowed to speak and who is silenced regarding the Fly Creek development.
- The city council obstructed the Mayor from doing her job, at public expense, and betrayed election promises by paving the way for a developer of Fly Creek Apartments despite promising to stop development there.
- Mike Turner's letter to the editor in the Courier (tabloid) was criticized as containing misquotes, fabrications, and reliance on anonymous sources.
- Mike Turner is married to Pam Caudill, a long-standing board member of the Fairhope Airport Authority (FAA), who is also a friend of Jack Burrell and Ray Hix, both other FAA board members with ethics charges.
- Jack Burrell blocked the Mayor’s choice for a FAA board member intended to replace Pam Caudill.
- On Dec 16, 2015, Dennis R. Bailey ESQ of Rushton, Stakley, Johnston and Garrett submitted an RFP for a lease on an airplane hangar to the Alabama Ethics Commission, including Exhibit C, an unsigned Ground Lease dated Dec 21, 2015.
- On Dec 17, 2015, a Ground Lease was signed by H. Ray Hix as 'Limited Guarantor', Joe McEnerney as FAA Board Chairman, and attested by Joshua P. Myrick; this lease differed from Exhibit C in title ('Limited Personal Guaranty' vs. 'Personal Guarantor') and omitted the security deposit refund clause.
- On Dec 28, 2015, the Memorandum of Lease was recorded at Baldwin County Probate.
- The Ethics Advisory Opinion (Feb 3, 2016) required any contract/lease between a board member and the Authority to be filed within 10 days of execution; the executed Dec 17 lease did not comply, while the unsigned Dec 21 lease was submitted on Feb 8, 2016.
- On March 20, 2017, Joe McEnerney filed an affidavit referencing the Dec 17 lease and Memorandum of Lease as executed documents, whereas the Ethics Commission confirmed the Dec 21 lease as the document sent for approval.
- Dennis R. Bailey was hired by the FAA to 'head off any Ethics complaints,' yet he had a conflict of interest since he submitted the conflicting Dec 21 lease in 2015 and shares information with his client.

AUTHOR'S ALLEGATION:
The author alleges that Mike Turner's letter to the editor is a false narrative designed to obscure the unethical dealings, manipulation of the RFP process, and false documents involving Jack Burrell, Pam Caudill, Ray Hix, and Dennis Bailey at the Fairhope Airport Authority, which have cost the city millions.

